# Privacy Policy - Check the Link

**Effective date: June 12, 2026**

Check the Link ("the bot") is a Discord bot that detects and deletes unwanted links. This policy explains what data the bot processes and stores.

## Data we store

- **Server settings**: the server ID and the configuration chosen by server admins (enabled/disabled state, logging channel ID, punishment type, feedback settings, and whitelisted channel, role, and user IDs).
- **Deletion statistics**: anonymous counters — the number of deleted links per user ID, per server, and per domain. These are numbers only.

This data is stored in a private MongoDB database accessible only to the bot developer.

## Data we do NOT store

- **No message content.** Messages are scanned for links in memory and immediately discarded. Deleted messages are only shown once, censored behind spoiler tags, in the server's own log channel (if configured) — never saved by us.
- No usernames, no DM content, no presence or activity data.
- Nothing is sold, shared with third parties, or used to train AI/machine learning models.

## Opting out

Server admins can disable the bot at any time or whitelist specific users, roles, or channels so their messages are never checked. Removing the bot from a server stops all processing for that server.

## Data removal

To have your server's settings or statistics deleted, contact us in the [Support Server](https://discord.gg/UM83TMsEGV).

## Changes

We may update this policy; the current version is always available at this page.
